From eedbc8769267c9e0053752de0e3d01da1d00759d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:25:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Listing photos from our own address: sized for where they
 show, kept 30 days

The MLS photo server allows 240 photos a minute for every visitor together and sends each one
full size, about 750 KB. Every listing photo now loads from /homes/p/card (about 480 px wide:
cards, rows, the map) or /homes/p/big (about 1280 px: the listing page). Each is fetched from
Trestle once, resized by Cloudflare when Image Transformations is on for the zone (kept as it
came otherwise), and kept in the edge cache and the browser for 30 days. A replaced photo has a
new link and gets a new copy; a sold home is not shown, and its copy expires by itself. Only our
own feed's photo links are served. When the MLS refuses, the browser is sent to the MLS and
nothing is kept. The owners decided this (2026-10-28); it replaces the contract's hotlink rule.

